 comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_live_dc_isolation_controls_59b2.py:1-14, 49-55, 104-109, 153-164, 186-193` — Preserve destructive-test isolation and explicit opt-in controls. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_live_dc_pass_health.py:1-22` — Preserve live DC pass-health classification and diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_live_dc_rekey_target_d582.py:1-11` — Preserve safe rekey targeting in live DC tests. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py:1-14, 230-255, 327-336, 409-420, 441-445, 496-499, 571-590, 649-657, 674-680` — Preserve destructive-run isolation, provisioning, ownership, cleanup, and credential-safety invariants. Consumer: live-test maintainers (the production fixture docstring read by this file is outside these ranges).\n- `tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py:1-28, 196-209, 217-221` — Preserve isolated project creation, teardown, and failure diagnostics. Consumer: live-test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py:1-18` — Preserve confinement of live Jira work under xdist. Consumer: live-test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py:1-21, 302-305, 346-349, 366-370, 397-400` — Preserve provider capability negotiation and fallback boundaries. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py:1-15, 219-228` — Preserve gate configuration resolution from the repository root. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_failure_classifier.py:189-198` — Preserve failure-classification precedence. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_failure_matrix.py:1-40, 134-145, 256-261, 271-277, 302-304, 382-385, 479-483, 502-508, 532-536, 586-588` — Preserve failure taxonomy, CURRENT marker tokens, and matrix completeness. Consumer: test maintainers and the self-source meta-test that counts CURRENT( markers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py:1-13, 113-122, 296-301` — Preserve ordered provider fallback and terminal-error behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py:1-23` — Preserve rejection/removal of legacy model environment variables. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_model_per_request.py:1-21` — Preserve per-request model selection without shared-state leakage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_provider_factory.py:1-25, 87-95, 207-217, 235-243` — Preserve provider selection, capability construction, validation, and errors. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_temperature.py:94-99, 118-127` — Preserve temperature forwarding and provider-specific omission behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:1-10, 99-106, 341-355, 405-413, 425-431` — Preserve layered timeout bounds and cancellation behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py:1-28, 141-154, 190-193, 281-284` — Preserve the lock-age ceiling, ownership checks, and stale-reclaim boundaries. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_container_recreate.py:1-26` — Preserve lock recovery across container recreation without unsafe stealing. Consumer: concurrency maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every 